# scripts/opcount: `sessionbench bench verify N` checks N tokens against a
# std session/memory store of 1024 sessions, each one SHA-256 of the token
# and one Verify (AU2); the cost of one check is the slope between the two
# sizes. The control is hand Go with a map of digests under a mutex and
# two time compares; the floor is one SHA-256 into a fixed array and one
# map read.
unit check
sizes 200000 1200000
args bench verify {n}
control benchmarks/session/testdata/control
floor benchmarks/session/testdata/floor
